  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations are $79.2M for Medical Laboratories (NAICS 621511) in FY2027 to date. Award count is 195 and average award size is $406K. Obligations fell 72.4% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $1.7B in FY22, $418M in FY23, $398M in FY24, $460M in FY25, $287M in FY26, and $79.2M in FY27. Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $79.1M in FY2027 to date. QUEST DIAGNOSTICS INCORPORATED is the largest vendor with $43.9M in FY2027 to date, followed by LABORATORY CORPORATION OF AMERICA with $21.4M. The FY2027 buyer list also includes Department of Justice with $229K and Department of State with $19.8K. The vendor list also includes ARUP LABORATORIES INC with $1.8M, AVMEDICAL LLC with $1.4M, and VANDERBILT UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER with $998K. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations much lower than prior years?",
